  "note": "Grade numbers are the mainland 1-10 ladder (央音 1-9 plus 演奏级, 国院 1-10, 音协 1-10; they differ by up to about two grades between bodies). ABRSM and Trinity do not examine this instrument. No board publishes ranges, meters or tempi per grade, so every number here is our inference from technique lists in exam books and teacher articles and from the Hong Kong LCSD syllabus; treat the whole profile as low confidence and a guide, not a limit. A 21-string guzheng in D is tuned to the D major pentatonic (D E F# A B) over D2-D6; the 4th and 7th degrees (G and C#) exist only by pressing a string (按音), taught from about Grade 2. Retuning to G, C or F arrives only at the upper grades, so the pitch-set check is switched off from Grade 7. A grand-staff part (right hand on top, up to four notes a hand) is read as one part. Techniques the checker can not see (摇指, 轮指, 刮奏) are listed in references/instruments/guzheng.md. See that file for the sources.",
